{
 "comment": "Scope membership pages (capability scope-membership-v1). A page keeps the pull envelope and one cursor per scope; each change names its scope and log cursor, with from < cursor <= to in that scope's range. An upsert carries the scope, cursor and kind beside the existing authority record fields (model, identity, stamp, state or error); a removal carries only scope, cursor, kind, model and identity. A scope holds at most 50 changes and a scope/record pair appears at most once, as does a scope position. Enrollment responses carry memberships claims {scope, cursor, model, identity}, each for a record the response returns, unique per scope/record pair and scope position. Requests advertise capabilities as envelope metadata that saved-call identity ignores.",
 "capability": "scope-membership-v1",
 "canonical": {
  "wire": "{\"changes\":[{\"cursor\":2,\"identity\":{\"id\":\"a\"},\"kind\":\"upsert\",\"model\":\"Entry\",\"scope\":\"U\",\"stamp\":1,\"state\":{\"text\":\"A\"}},{\"cursor\":3,\"identity\":{\"id\":\"b\"},\"kind\":\"remove\",\"model\":\"Entry\",\"scope\":\"U\"}],\"cursors\":{\"U\":{\"from\":1,\"head\":3,\"to\":3}}}",
  "scopes": [
   "U"
  ],
  "kinds": [
   "upsert",
   "remove"
  ]
 },
